            <ArticleTitle>The effect of ketamine pretreatment on propofol injection pain in 100 women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>302-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A controlled, randomised double-blind study was performed to compare the prior intravenous administration of ketamine 10 mg (1 ml) or 0.9% saline (1 ml) on propofol injection pain. One hundred patients of ASA status 1 or 2 presenting for gynaecological surgery were studied. Following an initial 5-ml bolus of propofol into a dorsal hand vein, 30 s after the treatment, 84% of the saline control patients experienced mild or severe pain compared to 26% of those who were given ketamine pretreatment (p &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
